1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,200
Communication isn't about saying more.
It's about being understood.

2
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:09,500
Welcome. Today we will explore 9 golden tips
to improve your communication skills and influence.

3
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:15,000
Tip Number 1:
Listen with intent instead of waiting to respond.

4
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:20,500
Most people do not listen to understand;
they listen to prepare their reply.

5
00:00:21,100 --> 00:00:26,000
When you give your full attention to someone,
you build trust and mutual respect.

6
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:31,500
Tip Number 2:
Use pauses to create clarity and authority.

7
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:37,200
A deliberate pause gives weight to your words
and projects wisdom and confidence.

8
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:43,000
Pausing allows your listener to absorb the idea
and prevents rushed speaking.

9
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:48,500
Tip Number 3:
Adjust your message to who you're speaking to.

10
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:54,200
A great communicator adapts their delivery
to match the background and needs of their audience.

11
00:00:54,800 --> 00:01:00,500
Speak in terms of results with executives,
and in terms of collaboration with peers.

12
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:06,000
Tip Number 4:
Simplify your language so ideas land cleanly.

13
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:11,800
The goal of communication is expression, not impression.
Simplicity is the ultimate sophistication.

14
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:17,500
Clear, direct words eliminate misunderstandings
and carry your point straight home.

15
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:23,000
Tip Number 5:
Build trust by matching words with consistent action.

16
00:01:23,600 --> 00:01:29,000
People believe what they see in your actions
far more than what they hear from your lips.

17
00:01:29,600 --> 00:01:35,200
When your actions reinforce your promises,
credibility and respect follow naturally.

18
00:01:36,200 --> 00:01:40,800
Tip Number 6:
Speak with emotional conviction and sincerity.

19
00:01:41,400 --> 00:01:46,800
Effective communication is 20% what you know
and 80% how you feel about what you know.

20
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:53,000
Words charged with genuine emotion and care
reach straight into people's hearts and minds.

21
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:58,500
Tip Number 7:
Master non-verbal communication and eye contact.

22
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:04,500
Confident eye contact, balanced posture, and open gestures
deliver more than half of your message.

23
00:02:05,100 --> 00:02:11,000
Ensure your body language is warm, welcoming,
and aligned with your authentic intent.

24
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:16,500
Tip Number 8:
Be brief and avoid overtalking.

25
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:22,500
Say what needs to be said without clutter or rambling;
excess words dilute impact.

26
00:02:23,100 --> 00:02:28,800
Keep it concise and leave room for the other person
to engage and respond.

27
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:34,500
Tip Number 9:
Never stop learning, reading, and expanding vocabulary.

28
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:40,500
Read books, take notes in journals, and observe great speakers;
communication is built through deliberate practice.

29
00:02:41,100 --> 00:02:47,000
The richer your vocabulary and understanding,
the more precisely you can express your vision.

30
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:54,000
Mastering communication changes how opportunities come to you,
because people trust what they understand.

31
00:02:54,500 --> 00:03:00,000
Apply these 9 principles in your daily life,
and watch your influence and relationships transform.
